# ---- the main-red detector reads the merge queue (2026-09-24, optional) ----
# Each tree is tested once, in the Mergify merge-queue batch; a push to main
# runs only the fast checks. So a main that breaks by itself shows up as every
# batch going red. bin/main-red-detector.sh reads the newest pull_request runs
# of the repos below (one more read per tick), keeps the required runs on a
# mergify/merge-queue/* head, and freezes merges (reason=queue) when
# MAIN_RED_QUEUE_STREAK batches that share no PR number are red with no green
# batch since. Stacked speculative batches share PRs, so one bad PR is never
# read as a red main.
#
# 1 is the default. Only the literal 0 disarms it: no pull_request runs read.
#MAIN_RED_QUEUE=1
#MAIN_RED_QUEUE_REPOS=example-org/cromford
#MAIN_RED_QUEUE_STREAK=3
#MAIN_RED_QUEUE_PER_PAGE=100
